-You can pass as many column-name column-type pairs as you like. Valid types are ``integer``, ``text``, ``float`` and ``blob``.
+Use ``--strict`` to create a `STRICT table
+<https://www.sqlite.org/stricttables.html>`__ (requires SQLite 3.37 or higher)::
+
+    $ sqlite-utils create-table mydb.db mytable id integer name text --pk=id --strict
+
+The ``insert`` and ``upsert`` commands also accept ``--strict`` when they create
+a new table.
+
+You can pass as many column-name column-type pairs as you like. Valid types are
+``integer``, ``int``, ``text``, ``float``, ``real``, ``blob`` and ``any``.
 
 You can specify columns that should be NOT NULL using ``--not-null colname``. You can specify default values for columns using ``--default colname defaultvalue``.
 
